-- title:
--   Nontriviality of W[[u,v]]/(uv-π) for non-unit π
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$ be an element that is not a unit. The theorem asserts that the ring $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$, defined as the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0, X_1]]$ (formally, `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed in the power series ring via the constant-coefficient inclusion, is nontrivial, i.e. carries a `Nontrivial` instance: it has two distinct elements, equivalently $0 \neq 1$ in it, equivalently the ideal $(X_0X_1 - \pi)$ is not the whole of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$. No hypotheses beyond commutativity of $W$ and the non-invertibility of $\pi$ are imposed; in particular $W$ itself is not assumed to be a domain, local, or even nonzero (non-invertibility of $\pi$ already excludes the zero ring).
--
--   This is the non-vacuity of the crossing local model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, the ring that describes the completed local structure of a modular curve with $\Gamma_0(p)$-level at a supersingular point of the special fibre (the case $W = W(\bar{\mathbb F}_p)$, $\pi = p$). It is used by the local-chart and level-structure constructions that exhibit completed local rings of the relevant moduli problems as such crossing models, where a nontrivial target is needed for the asserted ring and algebra equivalences to be meaningful.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_nontrivial_of_not_isUnit.lean

